From: Brian 'redbeard' Harrington <redbeard@dead-city.org>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: ccu-k3: fix transposed div/mux/fc/gate fields in RPMI consumer clocks

Value audit of 0003 against Linux ccu-k3.c and the K3 clock/reset manual
found three clocks with transposed field layouts. The Linux macro
argument order is div-first (CCU_MUX_DIV_GATE_FC_DEFINE takes DIV
shift/width, FC, then MUX shift/width, then GATE); the ported values
passed those numbers to the ESOS macros in swapped positions:

- ufs_aclk (APMU_UFS_CLK_RES_CTRL 0x268): every field transposed. The
  ported definition (div 4:2, fc BIT(1), mux 7:5, gate BIT(8)) maps onto
  the manual's UFS_ACLK_SEL, UFS_ACLK_EN, UFS_ACLK_DIV and UFS_ACLK_FC_REQ
  fields respectively. Correct: div 7:5, fc BIT(8) (FC_REQ), mux 4:2
  (SEL), gate BIT(1) (ACLK_EN). As ported, an RPMI enable would write
  the W1C frequency-change-request bit while leaving ACLK_EN cleared,
  and a rate change would rewrite the source select as the divider.

- sdh0_clk (APMU_SDH0_CLK_RES_CTRL 0x054): div and mux transposed.
  Correct: div 8:3, mux 5:3 (fc BIT(11), gate BIT(4) were right).

- axi_clk (APMU_ACLK_CLK_CTRL 0x388): mux given the divider position
  (1,2 instead of 0,1) and a spurious gate on BIT(0), which is ACLK_SEL
  per the manual — an RPMI enable/disable of axi_clk would flip the AXI
  source between 307 and 409 MHz. Linux models axi_clk with no gate; use
  the gate-less SPACEMIT_CCU_DIV_FC_MUX variant. div (1,2) and fc BIT(4)
  match the manual (ACLK_DIV 2:1, ACLK_FC_REQ BIT(4)).

apb_clk, twsi0_clk, all simple gates, ufs_refclk and every register
offset were verified correct against Linux, the manual, and in-situ
hardware validation (EMAC0 0x3e4, USB 0x5c, APBC GPIO 0x08, PLL2 SWCR2
0x11c bits 5/7).

Audit reference: Linux drivers/clk/spacemit/ccu-k3.c and
include/soc/spacemit/k3-syscon.h verified unmodified for these
definitions against the pristine 6.12.0-284 tarball; K3 user manual
chapter 17 (PMU_UFS_CLK_RST_CTRL, PMUA_ACLK_CTRL, APBS_PLL2_SWCR2).
diff --git a/bsp/spacemit/drivers/clk/ccu-spacemit-k3.c b/bsp/spacemit/drivers/clk/ccu-spacemit-k3.c
index 851adcb..c895301 100644
--- a/bsp/spacemit/drivers/clk/ccu-spacemit-k3.c
+++ b/bsp/spacemit/drivers/clk/ccu-spacemit-k3.c
@@ -817,11 +817,10 @@ static SPACEMIT_CCU_MUX(apb_clk, "apb_clk", apb_parents,
 static const char * const axi_parents[] = {
 	"pll1_d8_307p2", "pll1_d6_409p6"
 };
-static SPACEMIT_CCU_DIV_FC_MUX_GATE(axi_clk, "axi_clk", axi_parents,
+static SPACEMIT_CCU_DIV_FC_MUX(axi_clk, "axi_clk", axi_parents,
 	BASE_TYPE_APMU, APMU_ACLK_CLK_CTRL,
 	1, 2, BIT(4),
-	1, 2,
-	BIT(0), BIT(0), 0x0,
+	0, 1,
 	0);
 
 /* APBC GPIO: func clock on vctcxo_24 (fixed clock from the rt24 DTSI) */
@@ -859,8 +858,8 @@ static const char * const sdh01_parents[] = {
 };
 static SPACEMIT_CCU_DIV_FC_MUX_GATE(sdh0_clk, "sdh0_clk", sdh01_parents,
 	BASE_TYPE_APMU, APMU_SDH0_CLK_RES_CTRL,
-	5, 3, BIT(11),
-	8, 3,
+	8, 3, BIT(11),
+	5, 3,
 	BIT(4), BIT(4), 0x0,
 	0);
 
@@ -876,9 +875,9 @@ static const char * const ufs_aclk_parents[] = {
 };
 static SPACEMIT_CCU_DIV_FC_MUX_GATE(ufs_aclk, "ufs_aclk", ufs_aclk_parents,
 	BASE_TYPE_APMU, APMU_UFS_CLK_RES_CTRL,
-	2, 3, BIT(1),
-	5, 3,
-	BIT(8), BIT(8), 0x0,
+	5, 3, BIT(8),
+	2, 3,
+	BIT(1), BIT(1), 0x0,
 	0);
 static SPACEMIT_CCU_FACTOR(ufs_refclk, "ufs_refclk", "pll1_d64_38p4", 2, 1);
 
